{
  "raw": {
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409856": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%)School of Economics and Political Science",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%) School of Economics and Political Science «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%) The University of St.Gallen and its School of Economics and Political Science are inviting applications for an Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in the field of macroeconomics. Candidates with a focus in applied macroeconomics are particularly encouraged to apply. Candidates should have (or aim to establish) a promising record of internationally recognized research and show commitment to teaching excellence. Ideal candidates have an emerging track record of internationally recognized research in leading general interest or field journals. Successful candidates will teach in our Economics or International Affairs programmes. Candidates should have a commitment to academic leadership and citizenship, including contributions to public discourse and outreach activities. Experience in the acquisition of third-party funding is a plus. The appointment is for 6 years, with an intermediate evaluation after 3 years. Based on the tenure track process, successful candidates can be promoted to a tenured Associate Professor position. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position per August 1st, 2027, or by mutual agreement. Interviews will take place online at the European Job Market for Economists (EJME). Short-listed candidates will then be invited to present their research and have an interview with the hiring committee in St. Gallen in January 2027. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Winfried Koeniger, Chair of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching and research statement, list of research papers including publications, identification of the job-market paper, and two reference letters. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by October 31 st , 2026. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 3 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409857": {
      "title": "Selectus",
      "description": "Selectus - University of St.Gallen Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen More English Deutsch Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht (100%) Law School «Ein Ort der Wissen schafft» – Als führende Wirtschaftsuniversität setzen wir in Forschung und Lehre weltweit Massstäbe, indem wir integratives Denken, verantwortungsvolles Handeln und unternehmerischen Innovationsgeist in Wirtschaft und Gesellschaft fördern. Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht (100%) An der Rechtswissenschaftlichen Abteilung (Law School) der Universität St.Gallen ist auf den 1. Februar 2028 oder nach Vereinbarung eine Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht zu besetzen. Besetzt werden kann die Stelle mit einem Beschäftigungsgrad von 100%, oder nach Vereinbarung mit 75%. Voraussetzung für den Stellenantritt ist eine Habilitation oder eine habilitationsäquivalente Leistung mit Schwerpunkt im Gesellschaftsrecht. Sie verfügen zudem über einen qualitativ hochwertigen Forschungsausweis, der das Gesellschaftsrecht in seiner ganzen Breite abdeckt – idealerweise mit Schwerpunkt im schweizerischen Recht, mindestens aber mit klarem Bezug dazu. Sie sind eine unternehmerische Persönlichkeit und haben Freude an kollaborativer Forschung sowie an interdisziplinärer Zusammenarbeit, insbesondere mit Kolleginnen und Kollegen der School of Management. Sie bringen Lehrerfahrung im Gesellschaftsrecht mit exzellenten Evaluationen mit und können sowohl auf Deutsch als auch auf Englisch unterrichten. In Ihrer künftigen Rolle beteiligen Sie sich massgeblich an den Kernveranstaltungen der Law School in diesem wichtigen Fachbereich bzw. übernehmen dafür die Verantwortung. Von Vorteil ist Interesse und Erfahrung in der Weiterbildung. Sie leisten einen sichtbaren Beitrag zu nationalen und internationalen wissenschaftlichen Debatten im Gesellschaftsrecht, unter anderem durch die Organisation von und Teilnahme an einschlägigen Tagungen, und bringen sich aktiv in die nationale öffentliche Debatte des Fachbereichs ein. Sie engagieren sich zudem in der akademischen Selbstverwaltung und universitären Gremienarbeit. Ein starkes Netzwerk in der Praxis sowie nachgewiesene Erfolge bei der kompetitiven Einwerbung von Drittmitteln runden Ihr Profil ab. Die Universität St.Gallen setzt sich für eine inklusive Arbeitskultur und für Diversität ein. Wir bieten einen Dual-Career und Welcome Service für unsere neuberufenen Professorinnen und Professoren (und deren Familien) an. Nähere Auskünfte zum Profil erteilen Prof. Dr. Peter Hettich (Dean Law School, peter.hettich@unisg.ch ) oder Faculty Affairs ( berufungen@unisg.ch ). Interessentinnen und Interessenten richten ihre Bewerbung bitte mit den üblichen Unterlagen (Anschreiben, CV, Publikationsliste, Nachweise der didaktischen Eignung [z. B. Evaluationen], Lehr- und Forschungsprofil [max. je 1 A4-Seite]) in elektronischer Form bis spätestens 20. November 2026 online über https://www.unisg.ch/professorships an den Rektor der Universität St.Gallen, Professor Dr. Manuel Ammann. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 5 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409858": {
      "title": "Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise SystemsSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for a Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups to multinational companies, providing excellent opportunities for research and industry collaboration. The new professorship will become part of the School of Management and strengthen the University's interdisciplinary activities at the interface of management, information systems, data science and computer science. We are seeking a colleague with internationally recognised expertise in one or more of the fields of Data Management, Enterprise Systems, Enterprise Architecture, or related areas. The ideal candidate has an internationally recognised track record of leading research in Information Systems, reflected in multiple publications in leading international journals (FT50), a strong pipeline of promising research projects, a strong international academic network, close ties with industry, and excellent teaching skills at all levels, including Executive Education. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the School's teaching portfolio in core areas of Information Systems such as Data Management. According to our claim \"From insight to impact\", the future colleague should convey scientific knowledge to students and have a significant impact on theory and practice. Depending on qualifications, the appointment will be made at the level of Full Professor or Associate Professor. Candidates for a Full Professorship are expected to demonstrate internationally leading scholarly achievements, sustained success in attracting competitive external research funding, academic leadership, and a broad contribution to the development of their field. The successful candidate is expected to play a key role in strengthening interdisciplinary collaboration between the School of Management and other schools, particularly the School of Computer Science. The position includes developing collaborative research initiatives, contributing to interdisciplinary teaching, strengthening partnerships with industry, attracting competitive external research funding (e.g. SNF, Innosuisse, ERC, EU or industry collaborations), and contributing actively to the academic community and the governance of the University. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of  Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter specifying the academic rank for which the applicant wishes to be considered, a curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements (max. one page each), a list of publications, teaching evaluations, two publications that best represent the applicant's fit to the advertised position, and contact information for two professional references whom we may contact should the applicant be shortlisted for the position. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr  Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 18 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 6 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409861": {
      "title": "Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship Technology and Information ManagementSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship Technology and Information Management School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track (Open Rank) in Technology and Innovation Management The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for an Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track (Open Rank) in Technology and Innovation Management. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups, small businesses to large firms to engage in research. The new professorship in the School of Management will become part of our dynamic faculty and will be invited to join the Institute of Technology Management (ITEM-HSG) and the Global Center for Entrepreneurship and Innovation. We are seeking a colleague with proven expertise in one or more of the key domains of Technology and Innovation Management, including Global R&D, Innovation Strategy, Digital Innovation, Open Innovation, AI-driven Innovation, Technology Strategy, or related fields. Depending on qualifications, the appointment will be made at the level of Associate Professor or Assistant Professor with Tenure Track. The ideal candidate for the Associate Professorship has an internationally recognised and leading track record in research in leading journals in the field of Technology and Innovation Management, reflected in publications in top journals (e.g. FT50), a strong pipeline of promising research projects, a strong international academic network, ties with industry, and excellent teaching skills at all levels, including Executive Education. According to our claim \"From insight to impact\", the future colleague should convey scientific knowledge to students and have a significant impact on theory and practice. The successful candidate will also attract competitive external research funding (e.g. SNF, Innosuisse, ERC or industry collaborations), contribute actively to the academic community and governance of the University, and strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration across the School of Management and related technology-oriented disciplines. Associate Professors at the University of St.Gallen are provided with a budget to hire a doctoral student. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements (max. one page each), list of publications, teaching evaluations, two publications or working papers that best represent the applicant's current research, and contact information for two professional references that we may contact if shortlisted for the position. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 20 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 7 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409860": {
      "title": "Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in EntrepreneurshipSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in Entrepreneurship School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in Entrepreneurship The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for an Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track in Entrepreneurship, including SME or Family Business. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups, small businesses and family firms to large corporations, providing outstanding opportunities for research and collaboration. The new professorship in the School of Management will be invited to become part of the Swiss Research Institute of Small Business and Entrepreneurship (KMU-HSG). We are seeking an outstanding early-career scholar with a clear research focus in Entrepreneurship, or closely related fields such as Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) or Family Business. The successful candidate should demonstrate strong potential for publishing in leading international journals (e.g., FT50), an ambitious and internationally visible research agenda, and the ability to build a strong academic network. The successful candidate is expected to conduct internationally recognised research, actively acquire competitive external research funding (in particular SNF, Innosuisse, ERC), and contribute to the further development of the research profile of the KMU-HSG, the School of Management, and the University of St.Gallen overall. Applicants should therefore demonstrate outstanding academic potential and the ability to develop into an internationally recognized scholar. The position involves teaching at Bachelor and Master levels in English. The successful candidate will contribute to the School's teaching portfolio in areas such as Entrepreneurship, Small Business Management, Family Business, and related subjects. We are looking for candidates with excellent teaching skills who are committed to developing innovative teaching formats and inspiring students at all levels. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae including list of publications, research and teaching statement (each max. one page), teaching evaluations, two research papers that best represent the applicant's current research and contact information for two academic references. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 21 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 8 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/postdoctoral-researcher-in-nlp-and-human-centered-ai-m-w-d/97f7ad1c-fa1d-43af-89a6-cd38f3f317dd": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d)",
      "description": "HSG: Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d) School of Computer Science Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d) Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d) 80 %\n            \n            \n                (limited from 01.02.2027 or by agreement) Your tasks Conduct research on user modeling and coordinate selected research activities within CREST-AI together with Prof. Christina Niklaus. Combine LLM reasoning with neuro-symbolic NLP to build interpretable models of users' beliefs, uncertainty and misconceptions from dialogue. Develop human-centered evaluation methods for personalized AI to assess how people understand and use complex information. Contribute your own research ideas to CREST-AI, publish at leading NLP and AI venues, and present at international conferences. Supervise master's and bachelor's theses and student projects. Support research coordination and academic service. Your profile PhD in computer science, computational linguistics or a related field, completed by the start date. Research experience in NLP, particularly LLM reasoning, semantic representation or user modeling. Strong Python and machine learning skills; experience with knowledge graphs or human–AI interaction is a plus. A publication record demonstrating original contributions to NLP, AI or a related field, appropriate to your career stage. Ability to work independently, take initiative and collaborate effectively within a research team. Enthusiasm for interdisciplinary collaboration, particularly with researchers in philosophy and law; no prior expertise in these fields is required. Excellent written and spoken English. German is a plus. The SNSF-funded CREST-AI project Help shape a new generation of language AI that adapts to people's understanding. CREST-AI brings together NLP, philosophy and law to explore how AI can help people understand, question and reason about complex information, using legal language as a challenging testbed. You will join the research team led by Prof. Christina Niklaus at the University of St.Gallen and develop interpretable user models that guide adaptive explanations. What we offer You will work closely with Prof. Christina Niklaus and her team, with room to contribute your own ideas within the project's research agenda and strengthen your research profile. A competitive salary, funded conference participation and access to project-funded compute time support your work. You will collaborate with researchers at St.Gallen and the University of Zurich, alongside a fellow postdoc developing complementary methods for conversational AI. Application Please apply through the HSG online application portal, submitting a single PDF containing: (1) a cover letter, (2) your CV with publication list, (3) one representative publication or preprint, (4) contact details of two referees, and (5) your PhD certificate or confirmation of expected completion. Review of applications will begin on 23 November 2026 and continue until the position is filled. We are looking forward to your online-application stating the job ID apply here Inspirational Work Environment Executive Education Network Family & Career Equal Opportunities Fit and Healthy Inspirational Work Environment At the HSG, as Europe's leading business university, we operate in an entrepreneurial environment where you will meet highly qualified, ambitious experts - both regionally and internationally. For example, you benefit from a modern IT infrastructure and, in our library via HSGswisscovery, from nationwide access to the wealth of scientific information available. Executive Education We support internal and external executive education opportunities. Our internal executive education programme offers you a practical, dedicated and didactically mature transfer of knowledge in the form of seminars, e-learning, coaching and collegial advice. We support task-specific external training and executive education financially as well as with regard to the time required. Network We promote our culture of cross-functional collaboration and create space for forging valuable relationships - also with external partners. Regular exchanges and internal events help to strengthen these relationships and make them long-lasting. Family & Career We provide our employees with flexible work time models with a variable number of hours per week. As a family-friendly employer, we offer part-time positions, 16 weeks of maternity leave and a subsidised crèche, as well as support with childcare during the vacations. Equal Opportunities The University enables equal opportunities for all employees and students. This applies to degree courses and work, as well as academic careers, university management positions and the reconciliation of studies, work and private commitments. We are committed to this with various measures in the areas of teaching, research, administration and the Presidency. Fit and Healthy We help you stay fit and healthy. In addition to our diverse range of sports activities at the university, most of which are free of charge, and campaign weeks for corporate health management, we also offer you fruit in the workplace. In our canteen you will find a wide selection of freshly prepared meals - from vegetarian to fish dishes - at discounted prices. Further information on working at the HSG can be found here. For job-related questions Christina Niklaus Assistant Professor How can we infer what people know, believe or misunderstand from dialogue? We combine LLM reasoning and neuro-symbolic NLP to build interpretable user models. Thomas Huber Research Assistant Understanding language involves more than producing fluent text. Connecting NLP with philosophy and law opens up new questions about meaning and reasoning. Your place of work University of St.Gallen «A place where knowledge is created» - As one of Europe's leading universities of economics and business administration, the University of St.Gallen (HSG), Switzerland, is committed to the education of over 10'000 students. The HSG is one of the largest employers in the region and provides an attractive and innovative environment for more than 3'800 researchers, educators and professional staff. Other Jobs Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d) School of Computer Science 80-100% Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht – Ihr Sprungbrett in Wissenschaft (m/w/d) Law and Economics 50-80%, 80-100% Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) 80-100% Share share-solid Share apply here"
    },
    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/postdoctoral-researcher-in-conversational-ai-and-llms-m-w-d/d3780d8c-fa45-4b9c-9aab-c9c4b7702dce": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d)",
      "description": "HSG: Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d) School of Computer Science Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d) Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d) 80 %\n            \n            \n                (limited from 01.02.2027, or by agreement) Your tasks Conduct research on conversational AI and coordinate selected research activities within CREST-AI together with Prof. Christina Niklaus. Develop grounded, adaptive dialogue systems using LLM post-training and reinforcement learning. Build and evaluate a conversational AI prototype through simulations and user studies. Contribute your own research ideas to CREST-AI, publish at leading NLP and AI venues, and present at international conferences. Supervise master's and bachelor's theses and student projects. Support research coordination and academic service. Your profile PhD in computer science, computational linguistics or a related field, completed by the start date. Research experience in NLP, particularly large language models, dialogue systems or natural language generation. Strong Python and machine learning skills; experience with LLM post-training, reinforcement learning or user studies is a plus. A publication record demonstrating original contributions to NLP, AI or a related field, appropriate to your career stage. Ability to work independently, take initiative and collaborate effectively within a research team. Enthusiasm for interdisciplinary collaboration, particularly with researchers in philosophy and law; no prior expertise in these fields is required. Excellent written and spoken English. German is a plus The SNSF-funded CREST-AI project Help shape a new generation of language AI that adapts to people's understanding. CREST-AI brings together NLP, philosophy and law to explore how AI can help people understand, question and reason about complex information, using legal language as a challenging testbed. You will join the research team led by Prof. Christina Niklaus at the University of St.Gallen and develop adaptive dialogue systems that tailor explanations to users' understanding. What we offer You will work closely with Prof. Christina Niklaus and her team, with room to contribute your own ideas within the project's research agenda and strengthen your research profile. A competitive salary, funded conference participation and access to project-funded compute time support your work. You will collaborate with researchers at St.Gallen and the University of Zurich, alongside a fellow postdoc developing interpretable models of users' knowledge and understanding. Application Please apply through the HSG online application portal, submitting a single PDF containing: (1) a cover letter, (2) your CV with publication list, (3) one representative publication or preprint, (4) contact details of two referees, and (5) your PhD certificate or confirmation of expected completion. Review of applications will begin on 23 November 2026 and continue until the position is filled. We are looking forward to your online-application stating the job ID apply here Inspirational Work Environment Executive Education Network Family & Career Equal Opportunities Fit and Healthy Inspirational Work Environment At the HSG, as Europe's leading business university, we operate in an entrepreneurial environment where you will meet highly qualified, ambitious experts - both regionally and internationally. For example, you benefit from a modern IT infrastructure and, in our library via HSGswisscovery, from nationwide access to the wealth of scientific information available. Executive Education We support internal and external executive education opportunities. Our internal executive education programme offers you a practical, dedicated and didactically mature transfer of knowledge in the form of seminars, e-learning, coaching and collegial advice. We support task-specific external training and executive education financially as well as with regard to the time required. Network We promote our culture of cross-functional collaboration and create space for forging valuable relationships - also with external partners. Regular exchanges and internal events help to strengthen these relationships and make them long-lasting. Family & Career We provide our employees with flexible work time models with a variable number of hours per week. As a family-friendly employer, we offer part-time positions, 16 weeks of maternity leave and a subsidised crèche, as well as support with childcare during the vacations. Equal Opportunities The University enables equal opportunities for all employees and students. This applies to degree courses and work, as well as academic careers, university management positions and the reconciliation of studies, work and private commitments. We are committed to this with various measures in the areas of teaching, research, administration and the Presidency. Fit and Healthy We help you stay fit and healthy. In addition to our diverse range of sports activities at the university, most of which are free of charge, and campaign weeks for corporate health management, we also offer you fruit in the workplace. In our canteen you will find a wide selection of freshly prepared meals - from vegetarian to fish dishes - at discounted prices. Further information on working at the HSG can be found here. For job-related questions Christina Niklaus Assistant Professor When should an AI explain, ask a question or offer a different perspective? We develop adaptive dialogue systems and study how these choices affect understanding. Thomas Huber Research Assistant The goal is AI that helps people think through complex questions. That makes understanding and critical reflection central to how we build and evaluate language models. Your place of work University of St.Gallen «A place where knowledge is created» - As one of Europe's leading universities of economics and business administration, the University of St.Gallen (HSG), Switzerland, is committed to the education of over 10'000 students. The HSG is one of the largest employers in the region and provides an attractive and innovative environment for more than 3'800 researchers, educators and professional staff. Other Jobs Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d) School of Computer Science 80-100% Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht – Ihr Sprungbrett in Wissenschaft (m/w/d) Law and Economics 50-80%, 80-100% Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) 80-100% Share share-solid Share apply here"
    },
    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/wissenschaftliche-assistenz-doktorat-im-steuerrecht-ihr-sprungbrett-in-wissenschaft-m-w-d/77360655-0fe0-4554-982f-c0a109441996": {
      "title": "HSG: Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht",
      "description": "HSG: Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht – Ihr Sprungbrett in Wissenschaft (m/w/d) Law and Economics Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht – Ihr Sprungbrett in Wissenschaft (m/w/d) Wissenschaftliche Assistenz / Doktorat im Steuerrecht – Ihr Sprungbrett in Wissenschaft (m/w/d) 50-100 %\n            \n            \n                (unbefristet, ab 01.11.2026) Ihre Aufgaben Steuerrecht entsteht heute im Spannungsfeld von Gesetzgebung, internationaler Koordination und Beratungspraxis. Bei uns bewegen Sie sich genau in diesem Feld: Als Mitglied unseres Teams im Steuerrecht beteiligen Sie sich an Publikationen, Forschungsprojekten und Gutachten im Bereich des nationalen und internationalen Steuerrechts. Ein besonderer Fokus liegt auf der Forschung im Unternehmenssteuerrecht. Sie unterstützen Prof. Dr. Raoul Stocker in der Lehre, betreuen steuerrechtliche Seminare und erleben, wie wissenschaftliche Argumente den Weg in die Praxis finden. Es besteht auch die Möglichkeit, eine Dissertation zu verfassen. Ihr Profil (Bevorstehender) erfolgreicher juristischer oder betriebswirtschaftlicher Masterabschluss mit sehr guten Leistungen Bei angestrebter Dissertation: Erfüllung der Promotionsvoraussetzungen der Universität St.Gallen Interesse an wissenschaftlichen und interdisziplinären Fragestellungen, insbesondere im Steuerrecht Neugier, Kreativität und ein Flair für gutes Schreiben Höchste Zuverlässigkeit, engagiertes Mitdenken, selbstständige und zielstrebige Arbeitsweise, Teamfähigkeit Sehr gutes Deutsch und Englisch in Wort und Schrift Das Institut für Law and Economics (ILE-HSG) ist in den Bereichen Forschung, Lehre und Weiterbildung tätig und finanziert sich zu einem grossen Teil über Kurse und Gutachten selbst. Die Mitarbeiterinnen und Mitarbeiter am ILE-HSG forschen an der Schnittstelle von Recht und Wirtschaft. Wir bieten Ihnen Eine abwechslungsreiche Tätigkeit in einem jungen, dynamischen und interdisziplinär ausgerichteten Forschungsinstitut und in einem Team, das Ihre Arbeit aktiv begleitet. Sie wirken an spannenden Projekten mit, haben Freiraum für eigene Forschung und die Aussicht auf eigene Publikationen. Ihre Arbeitszeit ist flexibel gestaltbar, und Sie können parallel bei einem Praxispartner erste oder vertiefte Beratungserfahrung sammeln. Wir freuen uns auf Ihre Online-Bewerbung gerne unter Angabe der Stellen-ID 2848 Hier bewerben Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld Weiterbildung Netzwerk Familie & Beruf Chancengleichheit Fit und Gesund Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld An der HSG als führende Wirtschaftsuniversität Europas agieren wir in einem unternehmerisch denkenden Umfeld und Sie treffen auf hochqualifizierte, ambitionierte Expert*innen regional und international. Beispielsweise profitieren Sie von einer modernen IT-Infrastruktur und in unserer Bibliothek via HSGswisscovery von einem schweizweiten Zugang zum wissenschaftlichen Informationsbestand. Weiterbildung Wir unterstützen interne und externe Weiterbildungsmöglichkeiten. Unser internes Weiterbildungsprogramm bietet Ihnen praxisnahe, engagierte und didaktisch ausgereifte Wissensvermittlung in Form von Seminaren, E-Learnings, Coachings und kollegialer Beratung. Aufgabenspezifische externe Weiterbildungen unterstützen wir finanziell und zeitlich. Netzwerk Wir fördern unsere Kultur der bereichsübergreifenden Zusammenarbeit und schaffen Raum für das Knüpfen wertvoller Beziehungen – auch zu externen Partner*innen. Regelmässiger Austausch und interne Veranstaltungen helfen diese Beziehung zu festigen und langanhaltend zu gestalten. Familie & Beruf Wir stellen unseren Mitarbeitenden flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle mit variabler Wochenstundenanzahl zur Verfügung. Als familienfreundliche Arbeitgeberin bieten wir Teilzeitanstellungen an, 16 Wochen Mutterschaftsurlaub und eine subventionierte Kinderkrippe sowie Betreuungsangebote in den Ferien. Chancengleichheit Die Universität ermöglicht allen Beschäftigten und Studierenden die gleichen Chancen. Das betrifft das Studium, die Arbeit genauso wie die akademische Karriere, die Besetzung universitärer Leitungsfunktionen oder die Vereinbarkeit von Studium, Beruf und privatem Engagement. Hierfür engagieren wir uns mit diversen Massnahmen in den Bereichen Lehre, Forschung, Verwaltung und Rektorat. Fit und Gesund Wir unterstützen Sie, fit und gesund zu bleiben. Neben unserem vielseitigen, grösstenteils kostenfreien Unisportangebot und Aktionswochen zum betrieblichen Gesundheitsmanagement bieten wir Ihnen Früchte am Arbeitsplatz. In unserer Mensa finden Sie eine breite Auswahl an frisch zubereiteten Gerichten – von vegetarischen Speisen bis hin zu Fischgerichten – zu vergünstigten Preisen. Weitere Informationen zum Arbeiten an der HSG finden Sie hier. Für Fragen zur Stelle Prof. Dr. Raoul Stocker Honorarprofessor / Direktor Sie suchen einen verantwortungsvollen Job und möchten an der Universität Gelerntes in die Praxis umsetzen? Dann sind Sie bei uns genau richtig. Wir freuen uns auf Ihre Bewerbung. Ladislava Metzger Administrative Institutsleitung Ich würde mich sehr freuen, Sie bald in unserem Team begrüssen zu dürfen. Bei Fragen stehe ich gerne zur Verfügung. Ihr Arbeitsort Die HSG «Ein Ort, der Wissen schafft» - Als eine der führenden Wirtschaftsuniversitäten Europas engagiert sich die Universität St.Gallen (HSG) in der Ausbildung von über 10'000 Studierenden und bietet als eine der grössten Arbeitgeberinnen der Region rund 3'800 Mitarbeitenden ein attraktives und innovatives Umfeld in Forschung, Lehre, Weiterbildung und Verwaltung.» Weitere Stellen Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP and Human-Centered AI (m/w/d) School of Computer Science 80-100% Postdoctoral Researcher in Conversational AI and LLMs (m/w/d) School of Computer Science 80-100% Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) 80-100% Teilen share-solid Teilen Hier bewerben"
    },
    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/head-of-programme-management-open-programmes-es-hsg-m-w-d/4a408c3c-8d7e-4eb3-b058-f49fcd26081c": {
      "title": "HSG: Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d)",
      "description": "HSG: Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Head of Programme Management, Open Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) 100 %\n            \n            \n                ( ab\n                \n                    01.12.2026, unbefristet) Ihre Aufgaben In dieser Rolle verantworten Sie das Programme Management der Business Unit Open Programmes und stellen gemeinsam mit Ihrem Team eine professionelle, effiziente und qualitativ hochwertige Durchführung unserer Executive-Education-Programme sicher. Gleichzeitig gestalten Sie die strategische und operative Weiterentwicklung des Programme Managements aktiv mit. Führung und Weiterentwicklung des Programme-Management-Teams sowie Sicherstellung einer professionellen und serviceorientierten Programmdurchführung Strategische Weiterentwicklung des Programme Managements mit Fokus auf klare Strukturen, effiziente Prozesse und Verantwortlichkeiten Steuerung der Ressourcen- und Einsatzplanung des Programme-Management-Pools und Sicherstellung einer ausgewogenen Aufgabenverteilung Kontinuierliche Weiterentwicklung von Prozessen und Qualitätsstandards sowie Förderung der Professionalisierung und Digitalisierung im Programme Management Enge Zusammenarbeit mit Programme Directors, Dozierenden sowie internen Schnittstellen, wie auch Marketing und Sales, zur Sicherstellung einer wirkungsvollen bereichsübergreifenden Zusammenarbeit Sicherstellung eines reibungslosen operativen Programmgeschäfts, frühzeitiges Erkennen von Handlungsbedarf und Unterstützung des Teams in anspruchsvollen Situationen Ihr Profil Höhere Fachausbildung oder Hochschulabschluss (Universität/FH), beispielsweise in Betriebswirtschaft, Management, Eventmanagement oder einem verwandten Bereich Mehrjährige Berufserfahrung, idealerweise im Weiterbildungs-, Event- oder Dienstleistungsumfeld; Erfahrung im Bildungsbereich ist von Vorteil Erfahrung in der Führung eines kleinen Teams sowie Freude an der Entwicklung und Förderung von Mitarbeitenden Erfahrung in der operativen Steuerung von Programmen, Projekten oder vergleichbaren Einheiten Ausgeprägtes Organisationsgeschick sowie ein hohes Qualitäts- und Serviceverständnis Kommunikationsstärke und souveräner Umgang mit unterschiedlichen Stakeholdern und Schnittstellen Strategisches und analytisches Denken verbunden mit einer strukturierten, lösungsorientierten und pragmatischen Arbeitsweise Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift Die Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) ist die Ansprechpartnerin für Weiterbildung an der Universität St.Gallen. Sie bietet ein breites Portfolio an Degree-Programmen, darunter verschiedene MBA- und Executive MBA Programme, sowie offene und firmenspezifische Weiterbildungen. Der Geschäftsbereich Open Programmes bietet ein vielfältiges Angebot an offenen Weiterbildungsformaten für Fach- und Führungskräfte und verbindet aktuelle Managementthemen mit praxisnaher Weiterbildung. Wir freuen uns auf Ihre Online-Bewerbung gerne unter Angabe der Stellen-ID 2836 Hier bewerben Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld Weiterbildung Netzwerk Familie & Beruf Chancengleichheit Fit und Gesund Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld An der HSG als führende Wirtschaftsuniversität Europas agieren wir in einem unternehmerisch denkenden Umfeld und Sie treffen auf hochqualifizierte, ambitionierte Expert*innen regional und international. Beispielsweise profitieren Sie von einer modernen IT-Infrastruktur und in unserer Bibliothek via HSGswisscovery von einem schweizweiten Zugang zum wissenschaftlichen Informationsbestand. Weiterbildung Wir unterstützen interne und externe Weiterbildungsmöglichkeiten. Unser internes Weiterbildungsprogramm bietet Ihnen praxisnahe, engagierte und didaktisch ausgereifte Wissensvermittlung in Form von Seminaren, E-Learnings, Coachings und kollegialer Beratung. Aufgabenspezifische externe Weiterbildungen unterstützen wir finanziell und zeitlich. Netzwerk Wir fördern unsere Kultur der bereichsübergreifenden Zusammenarbeit und schaffen Raum für das Knüpfen wertvoller Beziehungen – auch zu externen Partner*innen. Regelmässiger Austausch und interne Veranstaltungen helfen diese Beziehung zu festigen und langanhaltend zu gestalten. Familie & Beruf Wir stellen unseren Mitarbeitenden flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle mit variabler Wochenstundenanzahl zur Verfügung. Als familienfreundliche Arbeitgeberin bieten wir Teilzeitanstellungen an, 16 Wochen Mutterschaftsurlaub und eine subventionierte Kinderkrippe sowie Betreuungsangebote in den Ferien. Chancengleichheit Die Universität ermöglicht allen Beschäftigten und Studierenden die gleichen Chancen. Das betrifft das Studium, die Arbeit genauso wie die akademische Karriere, die Besetzung universitärer Leitungsfunktionen oder die Vereinbarkeit von Studium, Beruf und privatem Engagement. Hierfür engagieren wir uns mit diversen Massnahmen in den Bereichen Lehre, Forschung, Verwaltung und Rektorat. Fit und Gesund Wir unterstützen Sie, fit und gesund zu bleiben. Neben unserem vielseitigen, grösstenteils kostenfreien Unisportangebot und Aktionswochen zum betrieblichen Gesundheitsmanagement bieten wir Ihnen Früchte am Arbeitsplatz. In unserer Mensa finden Sie eine breite Auswahl an frisch zubereiteten Gerichten – von vegetarischen Speisen bis hin zu Fischgerichten – zu vergünstigten Preisen. Weitere Informationen zum Arbeiten an der HSG finden Sie hier. Für Fragen zur Stelle Dr. Cornel Germann Leiter Open Programmes ES HSG Ich freue mich auf eine Person, die Verantwortung übernimmt, das Programme Management weiterentwickelt und mit uns etwas bewegen möchte. Sarah Banzer Mehling HR Leitung ES HSG Du arbeitest gerne mit Menschen und möchtest deine Erfahrung in das vielseitige Weiterbildungsumfeld der ES-HSG einbringen? Ich freue mich darauf, dich kennenzulernen. Ihr Arbeitsort Die HSG «Ein Ort, der Wissen schafft» - Als eine